spring is here which can only mean one  thing mlb the show is back with plenty  of changes for this year's entry here's  everything to know about mlb the show  22. keep your eyes peeled to the channel  as we'll have an official review coming  up real soon and you won't want to miss  it  alright let's get the biggest changes to  the plate first right off the bat  players will have the ability to play  mlb the show 22 on the nintendo switch  the decision to bring the show to  nintendo switch means you can take your  progress with you on the go if you so  choose for the best graphics though you  might opt for the game current gen if  you have a ps5 or series x the baseball  simulator brings a significant amount of  gameplay improvements this time around  starting with custom practice a mode  that i'm definitely going to grow  familiar with in custom practice you can  lock in a certain scenario like let's  say a potential dinger to the center  field then replay it as long as you want  practicing that scenario and testing out  different defensive plays it's a  fascinating change that newer or amateur  players might appreciate especially with  how in-depth the show's gameplay can be  now mlb the show 22 has improved several  aspects of gameplay as the show tends to  balance video game heroics with realism  for example defensive fielding continues  with improvements to animations and  rewarding players who field perfect  balls the better timing you have the  greater chance you'll make a wicked  throw from the outfield in time to tag a  batter out or to pull off an excellent  defensive double play  in the past perfect throws were  exclusive to outfielders trying to cut  off runners but now perfect throws work  for infielders as well so if you have a  stud shortstop you can feel the perfect  throw to home with arm accuracy  dictating the window that you have to  make that play visual changes will also  affect gameplay like dynamic pci range  now the pci is this visual hud indicator  that players will use to adjust their  swing whenever they're trying to hit a  pitch and the pci will shrink now when  near the edge of the strike zone giving  an advantage to pitchers and reducing  lengthy at-bats cause in the past plenty  of at-bats would lead to foul ball after  foul ball drawing out the inning which  could become exhausting but with the new  pci changes there should be more  realistic scenarios playing out when  batting additionally now you can anchor  the pci to certain zones in the strike  zone when batting which will adjust the  sensitivity of your reticle anchoring  the pci will help narrow down with finer  controls on the sides and corners of the  strike zone letting advanced users have  more options on how they want to hit the  show has different game editions and  various upgrade paths which feature  cover athlete shohei otani aka showtime  enjoy a dope stylized cover representing  shohei's love for manga and anime for  those going after the mvp or digital  deluxe editions illustrator takashi  okazaki who according to san diego  studios is also a huge shohei fan went  all out the final result has a wicked  cool manga look to the cover art  now purchasing the more expensive  editions will net you several player  packs of different rarities for diamond  dynasty which is mlb the show's kind of  fantasy team mode but suppose the card  collecting fantasy draft style team in  the diamond dynasty mode isn't your cup  of tea well that's fine because in that  case you can always hop into the several  other game modes offered in mlb the show  22 from classic exhibition matches  between current rosters to simulating a  proper franchise experience in franchise  mode there's also march to october which  always has been kind of like a franchise  light mode except this time around it's  getting some pretty beefy features for  starters march to october will span  multiple seasons now you'll be able to  take your team to a successful season  more than once before having to  transition it into a save in franchise  mode now this gives particularly newer  players a really nice entry point into  playing franchise mode without  overwhelming them while keeping the  march to october experience lengthy  trade logic has been adjusted and  improved upon in march to october as  well now when it comes to trade logic  there's a lot of information that really  only matters to more hardcore players  but the surface level adjustments are  basically adjusting how each baseball  player is valued the show refined trade  block logic to better reflect current  trends and now teams will value top  players by placing a premium on them  when negotiating trades for example some  teams will value relief or closing  pitchers less when compared to starting  position players or starting pitchers  additionally players will no longer be  traded immediately after signing in the  off-season in past that will be the show  games you could create customizable ball  players and take him on the road to the  show mode now both of those will return  with changes based on community feedback  so last year fans weren't really that  excited that you could only have one  customizable ball player which mlb the  show 22 addresses by completely removing  that cap instead of just one now you can  have up to 10 ball players with  different appearances positions and  various play styles such as archetypes  you can have ball players dedicate their  attributes to things like power contact  fielding and so on the show will also  have online co-op another first for the  series allowing players to partake in  2v2 and even 3v3 matches this  functionality even extends to diamond  dynasty letting you combine your card  collection with that of a friend for the  ultimate stacked team  one thing fans are always looking for  are new legends and the show 22  introduced some new additions to the  legends roster including randy johnson  and his kick-ass mustache and joe maurer  to name a few there's a full list  available online and be sure to let me  know in the comments which legend you  are most excited to see return  customization also takes some steps  forward as well as you are now no longer  restricted to only using existing mlb  teams like you were in the past this  time around march to october will have  full team customization options this  year letting you choose a custom name  access the logo vault and even use the  stadium creator ballpark lastly the game  will have a completely brand new  commentary team as well john buxiambi  and chris singleton will be joining the  game as the new play-by-play and color  commentary voices with thousands upon  thousands of lines of audio recorded  setting up a complete redesign of how  the game is called from game intros to  epic home run calls and even post play  analysis just to name a few there's also  an aim to make the commentary kind of  more conversational and natural where  the banner between the two commentators  are meant to feel more integrated in a  seamless way with the live action that  you will see of each game so many of  these changes are explored at length at  the sony san diego youtube channel so if  you've got that mlb itch and you can't  wait until launch be sure to check out  those conversations with ramon and the  rest of the team mlb the show 22 is out  on april 5th on xbox one xbox series snx  playstation 4 playstation 5 and the  nintendo switch  you'll have the option of grabbing the  standard edition mvp and digital deluxe  versions depending on your interests now  don't forget to stick with gamespot for  our upcoming review of mlb the show 22.  now here's a quick gameplay snippet of  me hitting a home run for you to enjoy  and that'll do it for me until next time  there's a swing and a drive  that's back  that one is gone  here's jed lowery  [Music]  you
 

